From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0450: skip_overwritten_transfers: a rectangle list's guest cull and polygon bits no longer block it; why-not log; poison check

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (S2 lever 4). The feature is Renan Queiroz's rexglue-skip-overwritten-transfers (already
  in the series, default off because "it does not do its main job yet"); the poison check is the idea of his
  launcher/dev/overwrite-poison.sdk.patch (TMPOVW) re-done as a cvar, nothing copied
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched file is ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: RenderTargetCache::GetOverwrittenRectangle (cache.cpp) screened a draw out when the GUEST had a cull mode, a polygon
  mode or a polygon offset set. For a rectangle list the HOST ignores all of those (draw_util::IsPrimitivePolygonal is false
  for it: no cull mode, solid fill, front/back offsets unused in both backends), so a title that leaves the bits from the draws
  before makes every one of its rectangle-list passes "kept" for nothing - the likeliest reason the tone map was kept 444/444
  times. Now only user clip planes (which can cut a part off) screen it out there. Cvars skip_overwritten_transfers_log
  (false: why each draw was cut or kept, once per vertex shader / pixel shader / outcome, with the registers read, and a
  10 s summary) and skip_overwritten_transfers_poison (false: fill what isn't transferred with junk, to see a draw that doesn't
  rewrite all of it). skip_overwritten_transfers itself stays off. Not built or run.
Bucket: REDO

0450-skip-overwritten-transfers-fix.patch (mcla-x86 ORC; S2 lever 4, $WORK/scratch/S2/REPORT.md)

What was known. Renan's note (patches/README.md, gpu-round2-2026-10-27.md): with the cut on, the tone map's draw (VS
1FAB9787BCA32D7C, PS E5EBEFAE4D165CBA: a rectangle list, 3 auto-indexed vertices, blending One/Zero/Add, all four components
written, no depth or stencil, no kill, viewport and scissor 1280x720, at EDRAM tile 720 over the scene colour's range from tile
1024) was "kept 444 times ... line 1455" of his layered tree, so its 0.91 ms (39 ms frame, 2-CU RDNA2) was never saved, while
some smaller post-chain draws were cut. His TMPOVW patch prints the __LINE__ of the `return false` that rejected the draw.

Why. That line is in the first screening checks of GetOverwrittenRectangle. The poison patch's own hunks put its `return false`
statements at 1432 (draw initiator), 1440 (user clip planes / cull / polygon mode / polygon offset), 1448 (depth, stencil, colour
mask), 1456 (write mask), 1466 (blend), 1474 (kill / alpha test), ...; his layered tree has the depth-read-state patch's 7 lines above
the function, so 1455 is 1448 + 7 (depth / stencil / colour mask zero) or 1440 + 15 (the cull group) or 1432 + 23 (the initiator),
depending on what else the layers added. [INFERENCE] The tone map's state as he recorded it passes the initiator, depth /
stencil, write mask, blend, kill, MSAA and viewport / scissor checks (he lists exactly those as its state), and the only screening
check not covered by his description of the draw is the cull / clip / polygon group at old cache.cpp:1538-1543 (series 84), so that
is the finding; it is not proven without a run, which is why the patch also logs the reason of every kept draw. The group is
over-conservative for the host, so relaxing it is exact whether or not it was the one:
  * draw_util.h:61-87: IsPrimitivePolygonal is false for kRectangleList ("the current geometry shader doesn't care about the
    winding order - allowing backface culling for rectangles currently breaks 4D53082D").
  * d3d12/pipeline_cache.cpp:1450-1487 and vulkan/pipeline_cache.cpp:1786-1811: the cull mode, the front/back polygon offsets
    and the wireframe fill mode are set only `if (primitive_polygonal)`; for a rectangle list: no culling, solid, and
    GetPreferredFacePolygonOffset uses only the parallelogram offset, which moves depth (an accepted draw has no depth test
    or write, and the vertices' z is checked against the clip planes in the analysis).
  So whatever cull_front / cull_back / poly_mode / poly_offset_front|back_enable / poly_offset_para_enable the guest left set,
  the host rewrites the whole rectangle. (A title can leave those bits as the draws before it had them; how this one sets
  them for the tone map was not recorded anywhere I could read.)

Change (src/graphics/pipeline/render_target/cache.cpp only; no header changes):
  * The screening check now rejects only pa_cl_clip_cntl.ucp_ena.
  * Every `return false` of GetOverwrittenRectangle goes through OverwriteRejected("reason") (a file-static pointer to a string
    literal; the CP thread only). 13 reasons: not one auto-indexed 3-vertex rectangle list or tessellated; user clip planes;
    depth or stencil used or no colour written; components not all written; blending not a plain replacement; pixels can be
    discarded; MSAA above 4x or no pitch; the vertex shader's position/kill depends on a fetch; a vertex killed / position not
    fully written / W not positive and finite; clipped by near or far plane; not corners of one axis-aligned rectangle or out of
    range; two vertices coincide; no pixel surely covered.
  * skip_overwritten_transfers_log (hot reload): for each draw that needed transfers (only with skip_overwritten_transfers on),
      skip_overwritten_transfers: cut to the rectangle 0,0 1280x720 - vertex shader 1FAB..., pixel shader E5EB..., 1x MSAA; RB_DEPTHCONTROL ..., RB_COLOR_MASK ..., RB_BLENDCONTROL0 ..., RB_COLORCONTROL ..., PA_SU_SC_MODE_CNTL ..., PA_CL_CLIP_CNTL ..., PA_CL_VTE_CNTL ..., VGT_DRAW_INITIATOR ...
      skip_overwritten_transfers: kept (<reason>) - vertex shader ..., pixel shader ..., <n>x MSAA; <the same registers>
    once for each (vertex shader, pixel shader, outcome) (at most 256), and every 10 s
      skip_overwritten_transfers: N draws needed ownership transfers in 10.0 s: C cut to a rectangle, K kept: <reason> xN; ...
  * skip_overwritten_transfers_poison (hot reload): after the ownership change, the rectangle that was cut is cleared to
    0x8040C0208040C020 in every colour render target of the draw (TransferAndClearRenderTargets with no transfers), so a draw
    that does not rewrite every pixel of it leaves the junk in the picture instead of a stale value that happens to be right.
    A picture with the cut and the poison on must equal the picture with it off.

Not exact until checked: skip_overwritten_transfers stays false. Check (frozen world, per Renan's harness: four shots a scene, on /
off / on / off, free roam, pause menu, title, driving, D3D12 at 1x and the 1080p preset): --skip_overwritten_transfers=true
--skip_overwritten_transfers_poison=true against off must show no differing pixel among the comparable ones; then the default can
go to true (the profile, mcla/profile/pc_profile.cpp, is the place for the MCLA title).

clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only of cache.cpp with the SDK's Release flags: 0 errors, the one warning that was there.

